WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:06.447
- Light is very powerful for me.

00:00:06.447 --> 00:00:10.614
Yet, it's also something that
I'm desperate to hold onto.

00:00:13.018 --> 00:00:15.891
It's going, ya know, the
lights are going out.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:19.308
So I'm struggling to hold onto the light.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:25.338
I was in art school in '79,
and the eye doctor said,

00:00:25.338 --> 00:00:27.544
"Mr. Erra, you have an eye disease.

00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:31.031
"You will be blind in 20 years."

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.613
And I said, "what?"

00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:33.992
You're telling me this bad news,

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:36.392
I'm gonna make the best
art I can ever make.

00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:39.475
God dammit, you know, I'm gonna do it.

00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.567
I see very bright lights, and
I can't see dim light at all.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.927
I've never seen a star in my whole life.

00:00:49.927 --> 00:00:53.750
For example, I was looking at
that view towards Manhattan.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.417
What I see is a very small area,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.184
maybe about half the size of my thumb,

00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:02.904
and all around that it's not black,

00:01:02.904 --> 00:01:06.792
it's not white, it's not
grey, it just doesn't exist.

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:10.959
That's how I see everything
else is just nonexistence.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:17.067
There are a number of visually
impaired visual artists now

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.842
and we do have a facet in the art world.

00:01:19.842 --> 00:01:22.951
(mystical upbeat music plays)

00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:26.462
Light painting is a process
where you use your mind

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:28.621
as much as your eyes.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.214
It's very long time exposure made in

00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:34.047
a darkened room with a flashlight.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:40.402
The person will be there and
I will turn off the lights,

00:01:40.402 --> 00:01:43.233
and wherever I don't
paint with the flashlight,

00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:45.733
it'll be black in the picture.

00:01:50.397 --> 00:01:54.523
The fear I have about
blindness is very strong.

00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:55.764
It's the feeling that

00:01:55.764 --> 00:02:00.428
my life will not be
worthwhile if I can't see.

00:02:00.428 --> 00:02:02.329
But, as a totally blind person,

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:04.975
I will still be able to
do the light painting.

00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:09.369
So, it is a comfort to know
that my work is strong, uh,

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.536
even though maybe in the future
I won't be able to see it.

